CORE
main.c
--no-malloc-may-fail
^the C library models in 'models\.dir' were not preprocessed for this target and these options; using the built-in models$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the built-in model is used: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The models are dumped with the default options and loaded with
--no-malloc-may-fail, which the models depend on (the manifest records the
target and the prologue of macros for such options): the directory is not
used, and the built-in strlen gives 2.
